# GARDEN LICENSE — ₹20 CRORE NET SALE

**Status:** Sale offer. No transfer is complete until the final agreement is signed and all required formalities are completed.

## 1. Sale and ownership

The owner offers to sell all Garden rights that they legally own or control for **₹20,00,00,000 (twenty crore Indian rupees), net of all applicable taxes**.

After completion, the purchaser is intended to receive exclusive, worldwide, permanent and irrevocable ownership of the included rights, with the ability to use, modify, develop, commercialise, license, sell and transfer them.

The sale may include Garden's original documents, designs, specifications, software, source materials, names, marks, domains, repositories and related assets, to the extent legally owned or transferable by the owner.

Third-party materials, contributions, open-source components and other people's rights are excluded unless they can legally be transferred.

## 1A. Proprietary modular business portfolio (Garden v16)

All rights legally owned or controlled by the Garden owner in the Garden modular business framework (BIZ-001), its industry templates and its individual business designs are expressly reserved and subject to this LICENSE, including HOME-001 (housing), FOOD-001 (food-chain operating system), FASHION-001 and PERFUME-001 when developed, and subsequent business designs recorded in the portfolio. These include the owner's protected original product designs, drawings, specifications, recipes and formulations as documented, operating processes and manuals, software, branding and inventions, to the extent legally protected and transferable.

No third party is granted permission to reproduce, adapt, implement, manufacture, operate, franchise, license, distribute, sell or commercially exploit these protected assets without the owner's prior written permission, subject to applicable law, lawful exceptions, binding pre-existing grants and third-party rights. Public disclosure is not a free-use or commercial license. Templates are not finalized businesses, and this reservation is not a patent filing, grant or assertion of exclusive rights over unprotectable ideas, independently developed methods or third-party brands.

The portfolio is within the scope of the existing ₹20 crore net Garden sale offer to the extent rights are legally owned or controlled and included in the final signed agreement. The sale price, purchaser priority, transfer formalities and existing restrictions remain unchanged.

## 2. Purchaser priority and transfer

Priority goes to the first eligible purchaser who completes both requirements:

1. The full payment required to leave the owner with ₹20 crore net reaches the nominated bank account as cleared, irrevocable funds.
2. The complete proposed transfer agreement and supporting documents reach the owner's nominated email address.

Reliable timestamps determine priority. An incomplete payment or agreement does not qualify.

The owner must verify the purchaser and documents and sign the final agreement. The transfer becomes effective only after signing and completion of all required legal formalities.

The final agreement must identify the assets, payment and tax arrangements, responsibilities, liabilities, handover process and applicable dispute procedure.

## 3. No unauthorized use

Nobody may use, copy, modify, implement, distribute, sell or commercially benefit from Garden's protected work without the owner's written permission. This includes indirect use and use through another person or organisation.

Anyone who makes unauthorized use and gains a benefit explicitly agrees to pay **1,000% (10 times) of the total benefit gained from using Garden ideas**.

The owner may seek an order to stop the use, claim compensation and take other legal action. Where the conduct is a criminal offence, the owner may report it and seek prosecution under applicable law.

This clause covers only rights the owner legally owns or controls. It does not claim ownership over ideas that the law does not allow anyone to own.

## 4. Final conditions

Before completion, the parties must verify ownership, third-party rights, purchaser identity, source of funds, applicable taxes and any required approvals or registrations.

The repository's default-branch LICENSE is the canonical published version. Any change requires the owner's express approval of the exact wording.

This LICENSE is a sale offer, not a completed sale, signed transfer agreement, tax opinion or guarantee that every Garden asset is transferable.

